  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increased capacity of the constituents to promote and support responsible business conduct to advance sustainable enterprises and decent work, including in supply chains</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The following are the major global deliverables and activities of the ILO in this policy area.
(1) Expanded ILO Helpdesk for Business with an ILO data platform relevant to support human rights due diligence processes.
(2) Enhanced partnership with investment promotion agencies on FDI for more and better jobs, including through the Community of Practice for IPAs on FDI for more and better jobs.
(3) Enhanced exchange of experiences on the promotion of the MNE Declaration among ILO member States, including national focal points, through a newly established Community of Practice on the promotion of the MNE Declaration.
(4) Launch of new packages on &#x201c;digitalization of the retail sector&#x201d;, &#x201c;responsible business conduct and gender equality&#x201d;, and &#x201c;role of MNEs in formalization processes&#x201d;.</narrative>
  </description>
